(2) READ/STORE INTERLEAVING UNDER ALIASING. Neither C parameter is `restrict`-qualified, so `out` may overlap `*m`, and this is a legal call. I disassembled the actual C .so (built with no optimization, CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE empty) and confirmed it RELOADS the struct field from memory immediately before EACH of the 16 single-byte stores. Excerpt for out[0] and out[1]:
```
mov -0x8(%rbp),%rax   ; reload m
mov (%rax),%eax       ; load m->a
mov %eax,%edx
