[38;5;252m[1m## The two bugs[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mMisaligned [38;5;10mm[0m.[22m The Rust did [38;5;10mlet m = unsafe { &*m };[0m. A struct at byte offset 1 of a heap buffer made it abort with [38;5;10mmisaligned pointer dereference[0m, while the C does an ordinary unaligned x86-64 dword load and succeeds.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mRead/store interleaving under aliasing.[22m Neither C parameter is [38;5;10mrestrict[0m, so [38;5;10mout[0m may overlap [38;5;10m*m[0m — a legal call. I disassembled the C [38;5;10m.so[0m (unoptimized; [38;5;10mCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE[0m is empty) and it [1mreloads the field from memory before each of the 16 single-byte stores[22m. The Rust read each field once and wrote 4 bytes at a time via [38;5;10mcopy_from_slice[0m, so under overlap it emitted pre-call values where the C emits progressively-overwritten ones. A dedicated test proves these rows aren't vacuous: the real C disagrees with a hoisted-load model in 4+ of 6 overlap offsets, and with [38;5;10mout = m+1[0m it produces a byte-propagation cascade only per-byte reloading can produce.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The fix collapses to a sequential single-byte copy, which is provably identical: since [38;5;10mshift == 8*(i%4)[0m selects byte [38;5;10mi%4[0m of the field at offset [38;5;10m4*(i/4)[0m, the byte the C extracts always sits at absolute offset [38;5;10mi[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
One judgment call worth flagging: I set [38;5;10mdebug-assertions = false[0m in [38;5;10m[profile.dev][0m. rustc's optional UB checks turned the NULL-pointer fault this library must reproduce into [38;5;10mSIGABRT[0m instead of the C's [38;5;10mSIGSEGV[0m. Those checks are absent from the release artifact a consumer [38;5;10mdlopen[0ms; disabling them for dev means the suite returns the same verdict under every profile rather than only [38;5;10m--release[0m. Reasoning is recorded in [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m and [38;5;10mERRORS.md[0m. [38;5;10mc_src/[0m is untouched — source checksums and timestamps unchanged, only [38;5;10mbuild/[0m added.[0m[0m
